{
    desc => q{t{char} moves cursor to column before target character},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/till_char_t`

**t{char}** moves the cursor forward to the column just before the target character. Unlike `f{char}`, the cursor stops one character short.

**Keys:** `tw`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0 (on 'h' of "hello world")

**after_tw.png**
- Cursor at col 5 (space before 'w' in "world")
- `t` stopped one character before 'w', landing on the space
- Text unchanged
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('tw');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_tw');
    },
}
__DATA__
hello world
